message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and identify the version used."
title: "Hierarchical Statistical Analyzer (ZetaStats)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Terreau"
    given-names: "Sébastien"
version: "5.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
# Zenodo concept DOI: represents all versions of this software.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19500564
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienleonmichel/hierarchical-statistical-analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/sebastienleonmichel/hierarchical-statistical-analyzer"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  GUI and command-line Python tool for hierarchical and replicate-aware
  analysis of biological measurements using one global factorial linear
  mixed model fitted by REML through R's lme4 and lmerTest. Supports fixed
  condition, treatment and interaction effects, random experiment effects
  or fixed experiment blocks, sample random intercepts and explicit full,
  reduced or custom random-effects structures, equal-experiment marginal
  means in fixed-block mode, Satterthwaite Type III and contrast tests,
  planned-family Holm correction, response normalization and transforms,
  and three-sheet Excel export with descriptive statistics and fit diagnostics.
keywords:
  - "hierarchical statistics"
  - "linear mixed model"
  - "factorial design"
  - "fixed experiment blocks"
  - "REML"
  - "Satterthwaite"
  - "Type III tests"
  - "Holm correction"
  - "biostatistics"
  - "replicate-aware analysis"
  - "nested observations"
  - "lme4"
  - "lmerTest"
